<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates continue upward trek.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates continue upward trek.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) continued their upward trek on Tuesday in anticipation of a possible hike in U.S. interest rates, traders said.</p>
<p>Only the 12-month rate was unchanged.</p>
<p>Dealers said borrowing rates on the U.S. dollar had risen in recent days ahead of a decision by the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee which is due to deliberate on the issue on Tuesday.</p>
<p>A rise in U.S. interest rates may result in higher domestic rates, prompting banks to adjust their swap rates.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  MARCH 25		 MARCH 24</p>
<p>    1 W		8 13/16		 8  3/4</p>
<p>    2 W		8  3/4		  8 11/16</p>
<p>    1 M		8 13/16		 8  3/4</p>
<p>    2 M		8  7/8		  8 13/16</p>
<p>    3 M		8  7/8		  8 13/16</p>
<p>    6 M		9  3/16		 9  1/8</p>
<p>    12M		9  9/16		 9  9/16</p>
<p>    VAL		26-Mar		  25-Mar</p>
<p>--LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
